WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.501
Prosecutors in the rust

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.269
fatal shooting case

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.972
plan to dismiss charges against the actor

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.774
Alec Baldwin.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.175
In the case of that fatal

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.443
shooting on the set.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.078
The movie set of Russ Baldwin

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:12.679
and a weapons

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.614
supervisor were charged

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.449
with involuntary manslaughter.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.550
You may remember

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.451
in the shooting death

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.986
of the cinematographer

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:20.987
Helen Hutchinson

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.355
and entertainment reporter

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.791
Chloe Mills is breaking this story.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.159
This is a significant move

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.360
by prosecutors.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.561
As I understand it,

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.530
there is still charges

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.400
standing against the codefendant

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:33.967
in this case.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.035
Can you tell us

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.704
where this stands and is it over for good

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.641
Well, listen, so what we are hearing

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.443
is that prosecutors in New Mexico

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.911
are going to be filing

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.645
those documents

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:46.880
today or tomorrow

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.282
ahead of a scheduled status hearing.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.383
And this is ahead

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.851
of what was supposed to be

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.986
a criminal trial

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:53.953
with Alec Baldwin

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:54.687
and who you said

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.655
the codefendant, Kenneth

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:56.556
Gutierrez, Reade,

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.491
who was the armorer on Rush.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.626
I want to read you a statement

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.660
from Alec Baldwin's

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.129
attorneys, Luke Nikas and Alex Spiro.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.297
They tell CNN

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.765
we are pleased with the decision

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.901
to dismiss the case against Alec Baldwin

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.203
and encourage a proper investigation

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.071
into the facts

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.372
and circumstances

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.074
of this tragic accident.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.809
So we know that the next hearing

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.178
was expected to take place on May 3rd

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.313
a preliminary hearing ahead of the trial.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:20.713
Unclear

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:21.681
if that is still

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:22.615
going to be taking place,

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.583
but this is a big moment

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.451
for Alec Baldwin.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.152
Alec Baldwin sat down with me

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:26.853
last summer,

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.922
and he adamantly denied

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.757
ever pulling the trigger.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.425
He said that it was anybody's

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:33.393
fault but his

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:33.793
but know

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:34.894
he cried in that interview

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.062
with me, telling me

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:36.796
that there's not a day

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:37.597
that goes by that

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.966
he doesn't think about what happened,

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.668
what happened to Helena Hutchins.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:44.204
And the irony of all of this news today

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:45.605
is that today

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.241
the movie Rust resumed filming

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.742
after more than a year

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.977
since Helena Hutchins died

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.079
there at Yellowstone

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.080
in Montana,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.783
filming for about 20 to 25 days.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.119
And so this is all happening

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.086
on the same day

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:00.887
to go back and film

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.689
that movie as part of a settlement

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.190
between Alec Baldwin,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.191
the production of Rust

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.026
and the family of Helena

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.695
Hutchins, the widower Matthew Hutchins.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.196
And that was just recently sealed

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.031
by a judge. But this is a massive moment.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.133
We haven't heard anything

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.100
from Alec Baldwin.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.503
We've reached out to the prosecutors,

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.070
the D.A.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.905
in New Mexico for further comment.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.039
And I just want to point out

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.174
that this comes about a month

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.809
after the special special

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.411
prosecutor, Andrea Reid, stepped down.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.180
And it comes after the D.A.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.083
recused herself from from this case.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.152
Chloe Melas, thanks so much.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.686
And please stand by.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.188
Quite a development in this story

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.456
we've been covering for some time.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:37.123
We're also joined

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:37.857
now by attorney

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.359
and legal affairs commentator

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.560
Areva Martin.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.761
Areva,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:44.731
as we understand it, this is a dismissal.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.832
This is a major development.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.132
The case,

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:46.566
no matter how it

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.867
no matter how you slice it,

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.936
but dismissed without prejudice

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:50.970
and charges,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.072
still stand against a codefendant here.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:56.176
Does that allow the investigation

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:56.676
and the case

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:59.546
perhaps to be resurrected against Baldwin

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.681
or is he free and clear?

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.017
In theory, it does, Jim.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.351
But I cannot imagine

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.853
that any district attorney

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:07.754
would resurrect

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:08.488
those charges

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:11.157
given this bombshell news today

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:12.926
in terms of dropping the charges,

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.460
the involuntary manslaughter charge

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.795
against Alec Baldwin.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.164
We know that the gun enhancement charges

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.666
that were filed against him

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.235
have been downgraded just this February.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.571
So I think for all practical purposes,

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.805
Alec Baldwin is out

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.807
of any criminal jeopardy

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.043
as it relates to this incident.

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:31.711
Remarkable move now.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.612
Now, you followed

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.547
this case for some time.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.549
What do you think the key was here?

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.452
What is your read as to why prosecutors

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:40.954
abandon this case?

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:43.723
I think

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.090
the thing

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:44.357
that we

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.693
can point to until we hear

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.194
directly from these prosecutors

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:51.097
is the recusal of the prosecutor involved

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:51.631
in this case.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.099
I have to imagine that the new person,

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:53.499
they came

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.101
on, maybe looked at this evidence

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:55.468
and said

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.370
there is not enough evidence here

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.805
where we can get

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.840
a verdict, you know, a conviction,

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.342
you know, at trial

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.843
we can't convince jurors

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.011
beyond reasonable doubt,

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:05.912
which is the standard

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.713
in a criminal trial,

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.181
that Alec Baldwin is guilty

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:09.749
of involuntary manslaughter.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:10.250
I can think of

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.017
no other reason

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.653
that a prosecutor would drop a case.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.754
No question.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.389
We should note that both Baldwin

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.191
and the weapons supervisor

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:20.426
did plead not guilty to this.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.127
Now, I wonder that

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:24.197
this would close down the criminal path

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:26.266
so far for Baldwin here.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.701
Are there civil liabilities here

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.837
that would still hang over his head

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:33.606
Well, we know, Jim, that

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.942
there's already been a settlement

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.877
with Lena's family

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.445
and that her husband, in fact,

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:40.413
is moving forward

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.315
with being one of the co-producers

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.049
on the movie

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.917
that's filming at this moment.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:45.952
So I think the

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.520
the biggest civil

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.555
liability or potential civil liability,

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.557
that case has already been resolved.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.359
So I think for all practical purposes,

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:56.229
a good vote is in the clear, so to speak.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:58.097
He has maintained from the beginning

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.299
that he didn't pull the trigger.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:01.134
He pled not guilty, as you indicated.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.802
So I think this is going

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.404
to wrap this chapter for him.

